# Deploy

Workflows run on `ubuntu-24.04` and deploy from `main`.

Website: rsync to `/opt/rayt-me/rayt-me-website/`, then `./remote-deploy.sh web` with `WEB_IMAGE` and `API_IMAGE` unset.

API: `docker save` streams `rayt-me-api:cd` to the VPS. Restart with `API_IMAGE=rayt-me-api:cd ./remote-deploy.sh api`. Compose must not pull `rayt-me-api` from Docker Hub and must not rebuild over the loaded image. `/opt/rayt-me/deploy` has no default compose file; only `remote-deploy.sh` knows the file.

Do not run `prisma/seed.ts` when `NODE_ENV=production`.

```yaml
# ❌ BAD — compose pull of a tag that is not on Docker Hub
docker compose up -d api

# ✅ GOOD — loaded image, pull and build skipped
# wrapper skips compose pull/build, then up --pull never --no-build
```
